Third-party material in this folder

Nothing in llvm-src/ was written for this repository. It is a copy of short passages from the LLVM project's source
code, and of what GitHub's public API answered about two LLVM commits and some release tags, saved so a reader can
check the passages that ../README.md quotes. ../fetch_llvm_src.py downloads all of it.

Source:  https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project, at the release tags named in each file's header (llvmorg-18.1.0 and
         later).
Licence of the LLVM code:  Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions, https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt. The copyright in the
         passages belongs to the LLVM contributors. They are included for reference only; the MIT licence of the rest of
         this repository does not cover them (see the last section of ../../../../README.md).

What the 19 files are:
- 14 files (the *.cpp.txt files, legality_*.txt, x86_cmpsel_cost_18.1.0.txt and x86_setcc_i64_18.1.0.txt) are excerpts
  of LLVM source. Each starts with a header line that says so and names its source URL and tag.
- 3 files (commit_39b0cbe69c.json, commit_b6a8f5486b.json and commit_in_tag.json) are answers of api.github.com, kept as
  the API returned them (saved as indented JSON) except for one change: every e-mail address in them was replaced by
  empty text. The two commit files hold the public metadata of those commits (message, author and committer names and
  dates, GitHub account links); commit_in_tag.json holds the result of comparing tags.
  The addresses were in the "email" fields of the author and the committer and in the same two lines of the
  "verification.payload" text, which is the signed commit object; there "Name <address>" became "Name <>". Nothing else
  was edited. Because the stored payload is therefore no longer the text that was signed, the signature in the
  "verification" block can no longer be checked against it; its "verified" and "reason" fields are GitHub's verdict on
  the original download, with the addresses in place, not on the stored text. Nothing in this repository reads the
  addresses or the signature: ../check.py reads only the author names and dates, the messages, the diff of one file and
  the tag results.
  ../fetch_llvm_src.py blanks the addresses in the same way when it writes these files. The addresses remain in the
  earlier git history of this repository, which this change does not rewrite.
- indvars_predicate_traps.txt lists line numbers and one matching line each from IndVarSimplify.cpp at three tags.
- collectLoopUniforms_sha256.txt lists SHA-256 hashes of one whole LLVM function (collectLoopUniforms) at four tags
  and two commits, computed by fetch_llvm_src.py; it holds no LLVM code.
